-- Named rejection: self-reference with no structurally decreasing argument.
--
-- M1 admits exactly one recursion warrant, a structurally decreasing list
-- argument, so that the promise "emitted programs terminate" stays checkable.
-- Widening this tracks LP-R7 (tabling / well-founded semantics on the swipl leg).
--
-- Two definitions, because the check has two halves and a fixture that exercised
-- only the first would let the second rot:
--
--   * `countdown` counts a NUMBER down. There is no list to decompose at all, so
--     nothing in the clause shows the recursion is well-founded and a target
--     that ran it would loop rather than fail. This one never reaches the
--     structural recogniser; it is caught by the self-call check on the ordinary
--     guarded-rows path.
--
--   * `shuffle sum` has exactly the right SHAPE — `CONSIDER … WHEN EMPTY …
--     WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest …` — and passes the whole list back instead of
--     `rest`. The decrease check is positional and syntactic, so this is the
--     fixture that pins it: a recogniser that only matched the shape would admit
--     a definition that never terminates. Note that the diagnostic names the
--     RECURSION decision rather than the table shape, which is why the recogniser
--     runs before `normaliseGuarded` (see risks.md §6 — `considerRows` answers
--     Nothing for every FOLLOWED BY row, so a check placed after it would report
--     "CONSIDER with a binding pattern").

@export
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`countdown` n MEANS
  IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE `countdown` (n MINUS 1)

@export
GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`shuffle sum` xs MEANS
  CONSIDER xs
    WHEN EMPTY              THEN 0
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN x PLUS `shuffle sum` xs

--   * `empty loop` puts the offending call in the arm the check used to ignore.
--     Only the STEP arm was inspected, so a self-call in the EMPTY arm was
--     admitted unchecked — and it lowers to `empty loop([], V) :- empty
--     loop([], V).`, which is directly left-recursive: not a subtle
--     non-termination but the textbook one, in the one arm no fixture covered.
--     The base arm may not call back at all; its scrutinee is `[]`, so there is
--     nothing smaller for it to pass.
@export
GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`empty loop` xs MEANS
  CONSIDER xs
    WHEN EMPTY              THEN `empty loop` xs
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN x PLUS `empty loop` rest
